-- title:
--   Reciprocity for $\mathrm{GL}(1)$: Artin reciprocity (class field theory)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ is a number field, $G_K=\mathrm{Gal}(\bar K/K)$ its absolute Galois group with the Krull topology, and $\mathbb A_K$ its adele ring. An **Artin representation** is a continuous homomorphism $\rho: G_K\to\mathrm{GL}_n(\mathbb C)$. We say $\rho$ is **automorphic** if there are a nonzero bounded cusp form $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_n(\mathbb A_K)$ with unitary central character and a finite set $S$ of primes of $K$ such that for every prime $\mathfrak p\notin S$: $\rho$ is unramified at $\mathfrak p$, $\varphi$ is right invariant under $\mathrm{GL}_n(\mathcal O_{\mathfrak p})$, and
--   $$T_{\mathfrak p,i}\,\varphi \;=\; N\mathfrak p^{\,i(n-i)/2}\,e_i\big(\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_{\mathfrak p})\big)\,\varphi\qquad(1\le i\le n),$$
--   where $T_{\mathfrak p,i}$ is the Hecke operator of the double coset of $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi,\dots,\varpi,1,\dots,1)$ ($i$ entries $\varpi$) and $e_i(\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_{\mathfrak p}))$ is the $i$-th elementary symmetric function of the eigenvalues of an arithmetic Frobenius. Equivalently, the cuspidal automorphic representation generated by $\varphi$ has the same local $L$-factors as $\rho$ at all $\mathfrak p\notin S$.
--
--   **Theorem.** Let $K$ be a number field. Every continuous character $\rho:G_K\to\mathrm{GL}_1(\mathbb C)$ is automorphic. That is, there is a unitary idele class character $\chi:K^\times\backslash\mathbb A_K^\times\to\mathbb C^\times$ with $\chi(\varpi_{\mathfrak p})=\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_{\mathfrak p})$ for almost all $\mathfrak p$.
--
--   This is the case $n=1$ of the reciprocity conjecture; the article states that it follows from, and is essentially equivalent to, class field theory.
--
--   **Formalization Note** For $n=1$ there are no proper parabolic subgroups, so the cuspidality condition is empty. The only Hecke operator is translation by a uniformizer at $\mathfrak p$, with normalising factor $N\mathfrak p^{0}=1$.
-- source:
--   Langlands program (Wikipedia article, uploaded PDF), section Reciprocity and section Status; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Langlands_program (Status: 'The Langlands correspondence for GL(1, K) follows from (and is essentially equivalent to) class field theory')

import Definitions.Def_LanglandsReciprocity_defs
import Mathlib

namespace LanglandsReciprocity

open NumberField

/-- **Milestone (the `GL(1)` case, class field theory).** Every continuous character
`Gal(K̄/K) → GL(1, ℂ)` of a number field is automorphic. -/
theorem reciprocity_gl_one (K : Type*) [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (ρ : Gal(AlgebraicClosure K/K) →* GL (Fin 1) ℂ) (hρ : Continuous ρ) :
    IsAutomorphic ρ := by sorry

end LanglandsReciprocity
